A Dma's end is connected through a frame without the right it needs.
A holder could have the controller read memory it may not read, or write memory it may not write;
the source is read and the sink written through a frame that allows it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: dma's end names no frame it may connect
Witness: fuzz dma-starts-within-its-frame

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -937,7 +937,7 @@ static int op_dma(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, const ui
         }
         /* The source is read and the sink written: the frame lets its holder do the one or the other. */
         struct cap fc;
-        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[2], CAP_FRAME, end == DMA_SOURCE ? RIGHT_R : RIGHT_W, &fc);
+        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[2], CAP_FRAME, 0, &fc);
         if (err != KERR_OK) {
             return err;
         }
